# T09 — Phase 1 — Identity resolution tests (renames, moves, duplicate names, branch changes, P99 budget)

**Phase:** 1
**Type:** tests
**Model class:** balanced
**Depends on:** T06, T07, T08
**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)
**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).

## Goal

This task delivers the full Phase 1 test matrix that the spec enumerates and the hot-path budget evidence that R10 requires. Spec §Phase 1 explicitly lists "tests for duplicate symbol names, renamed files, moved sections, and branch changes" and the DoD states "identity resolution adds no more than 2ms P99 to hot-path tool calls". This task creates two test files: `resolver_tests.rs` (correctness matrix) and `budget_tests.rs` (P99 measurement under an `#[ignore]` gate so a normal `cargo test` is fast and the slow budget tests run on the review pass).

## Spec excerpts that drive this task

> "Phase 1 Deliverables: ... tests for duplicate symbol names, renamed files, moved sections, and branch changes."

> "Definition of done: ... identity resolution adds no more than 2ms P99 to hot-path tool calls."

## Inputs

- Dependency outputs:
  - T06 identity types.
  - T07 resolver and ambiguity modules.
  - T08 serialization and RPC wiring (budget tests measure resolver calls as they are exercised through the same paths the MCP tools take).
  - T04 baseline metrics (`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json`) — budget tests assert the delta vs. baseline.
- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` (fixture conventions to mirror)
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/parser/` (used to construct realistic fixtures with multiple symbols sharing a name)
- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (one test per behavior, test reads like a spec, no fixtures larger than the assertion), `AGENTS.md` (do not regress baseline timings while measuring).

## Steps

1. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver_tests.rs` covering the spec test matrix. One test per behavior:
   - `test_resolve_path_unique_returns_fileid`
   - `test_resolve_path_after_file_rename_returns_new_id`
   - `test_resolve_path_after_file_rename_legacy_name_returns_via_compat_shim`
   - `test_resolve_symbol_unique_returns_symbolid`
   - `test_resolve_symbol_duplicate_name_returns_ambiguous_with_disambiguation_hint`
   - `test_resolve_section_after_heading_rename_returns_new_id`
   - `test_resolve_section_after_section_move_returns_new_id`
   - `test_resolve_symbol_on_different_branch_returns_branch_scoped_id`
   - `test_resolve_event_ref_round_trips_through_encoding`
   - `test_resolve_legacy_symbol_name_routes_via_default_workspace`
2. Each test constructs a minimal in-memory or tempdir fixture using the existing parser to populate a tiny graph; assertions verify the exact `ResolveOutcome` variant and the disambiguation hint content.
3. Add a `helpers` submodule (inline) with a fixture builder that other identity tests can reuse — single source of truth for fixture construction.
4. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/budget_tests.rs` with the P99 measurement. Each budget test is marked `#[ignore]` so a default `cargo test` stays fast and the review runs them with `-- --include-ignored`.
   - `test_resolve_symbol_p99_within_2ms_budget` — runs 10,000 lookups, computes p99, asserts ≤2ms.
   - `test_resolve_path_p99_within_2ms_budget`
   - `test_resolve_section_p99_within_2ms_budget`
   - `test_resolver_does_not_regress_baseline_workflow_p99` — exercises the resolver through the same hot path as `prepare_change` and asserts the delta vs. `baseline_metrics.json` is ≤2ms.
5. Each budget test loads `baseline_metrics.json` from the fixed path, computes the new p99, and asserts the delta with a clear failure message naming the baseline number and the observed number.
6. Add module declarations in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs`: `#[cfg(test)] mod resolver_tests;` and `#[cfg(test)] mod budget_tests;`.
7. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver_tests` (fast tests) and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::budget_tests -- --include-ignored` (budget tests) to confirm green.

## Files expected

- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver_tests.rs` — full correctness matrix for renames, moves, duplicates, branch changes, legacy compat.
- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/budget_tests.rs` — `#[ignore]`-gated P99 measurement tests asserting ≤2ms resolver budget and no regression vs. baseline.

## Verification

- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver_tests.rs` — confirms the resolver test file exists.
- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/budget_tests.rs` — confirms the budget test file exists.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver_tests` — confirms the correctness matrix passes; every named test must pass.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::budget_tests -- --include-ignored` — confirms the budget tests pass with the `#[ignore]` gate lifted; passing means the resolver is within the 2ms P99 budget defined in spec §Phase 1 DoD.

## Coding-standard checks

- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver_tests.rs daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/budget_tests.rs`).
- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — applies to every test function and fixture helper.
- Test length ≤30 lines per `coding.md` test discipline — extract fixture builders into the `helpers` submodule when setup grows.
- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.
- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.
- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming — test names read as behavior specs (`test_resolve_symbol_duplicate_name_returns_ambiguous_with_disambiguation_hint`, not `test_resolve_1`).
- For schema changes: not applicable.
- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec in a module-level doc comment naming the four spec-mandated test categories (renames, moves, duplicate names, branch changes) and the 2ms P99 budget.

